@startuml
' issue #2679 (follow-up): when both the legacy flat "groupHeader" and the
' new nested "group { header {...} } }" set a property, the nested one wins
' -- but only for the properties it actually sets. Here the nested rule only
' overrides FontColor; FontSize and BackGroundColor must still come from the
' flat rule, proving this is a per-property override, not an all-or-nothing
' replacement.
<style>
sequenceDiagram {
  groupHeader {
    FontColor blue
    BackGroundColor lightyellow
    FontSize 20
  }
  group {
    header {
      FontColor red
    }
  }
}
</style>
participant A
participant B

group Setup
A -> B: hello
end
@enduml
